                        "content": "A client is admitted to the hospital with a diagnosis of pheochromocytoma. The nurse would check which item to detect the primary manifestation of this disorder?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nHypertension is the major symptom associated with pheochromocytoma and is assessed by taking the client's blood pressure. Glycosuria, weight loss, and diaphoresis are other clinical manifestations of pheochromocytoma; however, hypertension is the major symptom.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nNote the strategic word, primary. Think about the pathophysiology associated with this disorder to answer the question. You also can use the ABCs—airway, breathing, and circulation—to choose correctly. One method for assessing circulation is to take the blood pressure.",
                        "id": "01fa7902512643e19211940dc561c8ce",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
