                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The nurse is caring for a client after thyroidectomy. The client expresses concern about the postoperative voice hoarseness she is experiencing and asks if the hoarseness will subside. The nurse would provide the client with which information?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nHoarseness in the postoperative period usually is the result of laryngeal pressure or edema and will resolve within a few days. The client would be reassured that the effects are transitory. The other options are incorrect.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nEliminate options 1 and 2 first because they are comparable or alike. Recalling that hoarseness that worsens is a cause for concern and may indicate increased laryngeal pressure or edema will eliminate option 4. The remaining option is the correct one.",
